# Chief Warg's Company is cast on turn 1. Its upkeep trigger makes a 2/2 Wolf token on each of Bot1's upkeeps (turns 3 and 5).
# (Ornithopter is there so that an attack is declared on turn 3 at all.) On turn 3 it is itself a Wolf and there is one other Wolf: that is one other Wolf, not two, so it can't attack (CR 508.1c; it
# does not count itself). On turn 5 there are two other Wolves, so it attacks, with the turn 3 Wolf (no longer summoning sick), and 5 + 2 damage is dealt to Bot2 (the token is a 2/2).

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Chief Warg's Company
Ornithopter
Forest x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Chief Warg's Company.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield = Chief Warg's Company; Forest; Mox Emerald; Mox Jet; Ornithopter; Wolf Token
! Bot1.Attack(Chief Warg's Company > Bot2)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield = Chief Warg's Company; Forest; Mox Emerald; Mox Jet; Ornithopter; Wolf Token; Wolf Token
Bot1.Attack(Chief Warg's Company; Wolf Token#1 > Bot2)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 13
Bot1.Battlefield = Chief Warg's Company; Forest; Mox Emerald; Mox Jet; Ornithopter; Wolf Token; Wolf Token
